description:
Design a clock divider module that generates a slower output clock (Clk_out) from a faster input clock (Clk_in). The output clock toggles its state after a specified number of input clock cycles, determined by the parameter 'count'. In this case, when the counter reaches 25,000,000, Clk_out is inverted, effectively dividing the frequency of Clk_in by 50, while the counter is reset to zero. This module is suitable for applications requiring a reduced clock frequency from a high-speed clock source.
module top_module(
    input Clk_in,
    output reg Clk_out =0
);

code:
module top_module(
    input Clk_in,
    output reg Clk_out =0
);parameter count = 25000000;
reg [24:0] counter=0;
    always @(posedge Clk_in)
		if (counter==count) begin
      Clk_out <= ~Clk_out;
		counter=0;
      end else begin
      counter <= counter+1;
		end


endmodule

